  "notes": "\"Drums first and drums loudest\" is the research's phrase and it is the model's thesis: `velocityTiers` runs 118–127 / 94–110, the hottest on this bench, over a 3–6-hit kick, a tightly layered snare at 1–4 ms and ghosts on three positions. Tom, ride and crash lanes carry the breakbeat and live-kit layers he imports from his electronic background — no other entry in this batch authors a drum-kit perc set. The 808 is aggressive and short (`staccato`, `heavy`, `distortionWet` 0.75, glides of 20–60 ms), the opposite of the Drake-orbit sustain. Harmony is a two-chord bed or a static tonic built from a chopped sample or one dark synth cell, so `impliedByRiff` is set with a low-weight `ii–v–i` for the jazz/soul-sample pole the research mentions on the alt-rap cuts. The arrangement is authored because the research names it: short intros, abrupt beat switches (`switchUpProb` 0.4), sub-2:30 runtimes. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium; the tempo band's upper reach of 160 covers his punk/electronic-leaning cuts but the mode of 145 is inferred.",
